## Business Rules

### Authentication & Authorization

1. All requests to protected routes require valid Google OAuth token via `ember-simple-auth`
2. Token is automatically refreshed before expiration via authenticator lifecycle hooks
3. Admin routes (`/admin/*`) require elevated permissions (checked via user service)
4. Session invalidation on token expiry or explicit logout clears cached data

### Chat & Message Handling

1. Chat sessions are identified by unique `sessionId` generated by backend
2. Each WebSocket message must include `type` field (e.g., `'user_message'`)
3. Server streams multiple answer entries; `onStreamEnd` event marks completion
4. WebSocket `onError` event triggers error state; `onClose` allows automatic reconnection logic
5. User messages are transmitted immediately; server responds asynchronously
6. Answer stream entries may arrive out-of-order or be retry-able on connection loss

### Data Consistency

1. Ember Data models remain canonical source of REST API data (users, sessions, metadata)
2. Chat messages are transient and not persisted via Ember Data; live only via WebSocket
3. All API calls must include authentication headers automatically (handled by adapter)
4. Stale data is invalidated on logout; cache cleared on session termination

